WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:08.280
We set sail on this new sea because there is new knowledge to be gained and new rights to be won,

2
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:13.440
and they must be won and used for the progress of all people.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:20.860
For space science, like nuclear science and all technology, has no conscience of its own.

4
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.000
Whether it will become a force for good or ill depends on man.

5
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.260
And only if the United States occupies a position of preeminence

6
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:42.800
can we help decide whether this new ocean will be a sea of peace or a new terrifying theater of war.

7
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:50.980
I do not say that we should or will go unprotected against the hostile misuse of space

8
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:57.380
any more than we go unprotected against the hostile use of land or sea.

9
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:04.640
But I do say that space can be explored and mastered without feeding the fires of war,

10
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:11.360
without repeating the mistakes that man has made in extending his writ around this globe of ours.

11
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:18.620
There is no strife, no prejudice, no national conflict in outer space as yet.

12
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.800
Its hazards are hostile to us all.

13
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.660
Its conquest deserves the best of all mankind.

14
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:31.020
And its opportunity for peaceful cooperation may never come again.

15
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.920
But why, some say, the moon?

16
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.660
Why choose this as our goal?

17
00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.220
And they may well ask, why climb the highest mountain?

18
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.260
Why, 35 years ago, fly the Atlantic?

19
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.540
Why does Rice play Texas?

20
00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.780
We choose to go to the moon.

21
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.400
We choose to go to the moon.

22
00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.700
We choose to go to the moon in this decade and do the other things,

23
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.400
not because they are easy, but because they are hard.

24
00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:13.740
Because that goal will serve to organize and measure the best of our energies and skills.

25
00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:17.680
Because that challenge is one that we're willing to accept,

26
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.800
one we are unwilling to postpone, and one we intend to win, and the others too.
